<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to July 9 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.44 (0.44)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.35 (0.34)	 two years    0.57 (0.59)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  1.01 (1.04)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.40 (0.40)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.52 (0.54)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.31 (0.30)	 three years  0.97 (0.99)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.35 (0.35)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.48 (0.49)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.26 (0.26)	 three years  0.92 (0.94)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Jul 07 - Jul 11:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.57 (0.61)   120-150 days  0.69 (0.69)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.60 (0.60)   150-180 days  0.72 (0.73)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.62 (0.62)   180-360 days  0.72 (0.73)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.68 (0.67)   over 360 days 0.90 (0.78)</p>
